---
# readability-magic-numbers: a sketch's pins, baud rate and test values read
# better as the numbers they are than behind names used once.
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables: a sketch shares its
# state between setup(), loop() and its interrupts through globals; the
# Arduino core gives it no other place.
# TimerTwo's own, for now: the groups that src/.clang-tidy turns off, until
# version 2.0.0 (OIL 3). clang-tidy holds a header to the checks of the file
# that includes it, so the examples would report the headers of src/ with
# every check; and they use the API of before.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  -bugprone-macro-parentheses,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -clang-diagnostic-unreachable-code-break,
  -cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -google-*,
  -misc-*,
  -modernize-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -readability-*
